PATCH 119 -- COORDINATED 0x7c8 scanline row-offset table pointer-scaling fix (DD2 "pointer scaling" class).

The DGROUP:0x7c8 row-offset table maps screen row -> byte offset (row*320) for every driver sprite/
glyph/rect blit.  It is BUILT by FUN_0000_0284 (mode-set init) and FUN_0000_02c1 (per-pitch) with
`stos ax` = 200 WORD entries at a 2-byte stride, but Ghidra typed the store pointer `int*` (4-byte
stride under gcc).  Readers index it at byte offset row*2 (WORD stride, e.g. FUN_0000_1091 the box
fill reads `rowtab[y0]` as uint16_t), so the mismatched builder made every reader see rowtab[row/2]
= HALF the intended row (the menu box/items sat at row 31 instead of 62).

Fixing the builder ALONE regresses because the still-`int*`-typed *readers* then read 4 bytes of the
word table and OR rowtab[row+1] into the high half (breaks the mode-set blit path FUN_0000_2fd7).  So
this is one coordinated change: builder writes WORD entries at word stride (0284 + 02c1), and the
reached reader 2fd7 reads a WORD.  FUN_0000_1091 already reads uint16_t (patch 060) -> now correct.
The remaining literal-0x7c8 / c794 readers (putpixel/getpixel 0edc/0efa, the sprite blitters) are not
on the menu render path (they retain their pristine base-lost form and are reconstructed when reached).

asm-verified: 0x2b5 (0284 fill), 0x304a (2fd7 `add ax,[bx+0x7c8]` 16-bit load).
